# The Cd panel is always the active configuration's drag stacked by source (skin friction, pressure, base, fins), in Aerodynamics and
# in Drag breakdown, with one configuration or several (the others are dashed total lines over it), dark and light.
# Run with the example, the two-stage example or a design of your own (an OpenRocket .ork is imported; a drive script cannot press Ctrl+O):
#   cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/analyze-stack.drive out/analyze-stack
#   BOWSHOCK_EXAMPLE=two_stage cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/analyze-stack.drive out/analyze-stack-two
#   BOWSHOCK_OPEN=/tmp/design.ork cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive crates/bowshock/scripts/analyze-stack.drive out/analyze-stack-ork
viewport 1300x800
click "Analyze"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot aero-dark.png

click "Drag breakdown"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot drag-dark.png

click "Prefs"
click "Light"
click "Done"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot drag-light.png

click "Aerodynamics"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot aero-light.png
